jobDescription:
Growe welcomes those who are excited to:

Analyze and tune system designs to identify and fix performance bottlenecks;

Analyze tasks, decompose them into sub-tasks, and estimate the development time;

Perform code & design reviews;

Lead research and POCs of new features;

Help with new architecture prototyping and migration on it;

Identify areas for improvement and manage tech debt;

Mentor and guide an engineering team of BE developers, fostering a culture of technical excellence, continuous delivery, and high ownership;

Support the current functionality and maintain backward compatibility for the releases;

Deliver completed tasks for testing and provide advisory assistance to QAs during testing.

We need your professional experience:

5+ years of .NET web development experience;

2+ years in a Tech Lead/Team Lead/Architect position;

Expertise and deep understanding of .NET 6+, ASP.NET Core, and C# technologies;

Strong experience with relational/non-relational databases;

Experience with a breadth of backend architecture principles and technologies;

Experience with asynchronous communication and event-driven architectures;

Experience with SSE, Long Polling, WebSockets;

Experience with Unit and Integration tests;

Experience with microservices architecture;

Experience with GitLab CI or other CI/CD technologies;

Experience troubleshooting production issues via an observability stack (Grafana, Tempo, Loki, Prometheus, OpenTelemetry);

Good understanding of software design principles (SOLID, separation of concerns, testability);

Good written and spoken English.

We appreciate if you have those personal features:

Proactive and result-oriented mindset;

Good communication and presentation skills;

Multitasking, time management, and planning skills.

We are seeking those who align with our core values:

GROWE TOGETHER: Our team is our main asset. We work together and support each other to achieve our common goals;

DRIVE RESULT OVER PROCESS: We set ambitious, clear, measurable goals in line with our strategy and driving Growe to success;

BE READY FOR CHANGE: We see challenges as opportunities to grow and evolve. We adapt today to win tomorrow.

Growe welcomes those who are excited to:

Deliver backend development initiatives;

Write clean, readable, maintainable, and well-structured code;

Coordinate cross-team interactions and dependencies within assigned initiatives;

Take ownership of received initiatives under the Tech Lead’s review;

Contribute to the reliability, performance, and maintainability of production systems. 

We need your professional experience:

3+ years of commercial backend development experience with C# / .NET 6+, .NET Core, and ASP.NET Core;

Deep understanding of microservices architecture and distributed systems;

Advanced experience with asynchronous communication and event-driven architecture;

Experience working with message brokers such as Kafka or similar;

In-depth knowledge of relational databases, including SQL, transactions, indexing, and performance optimization; PostgreSQL is an advantage;

Advanced experience with ORM tools, such as Entity Framework;

Experience writing unit and integration tests;

Advanced knowledge of authentication and authorization, including OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect;

Understanding of software design principles, including SOLID, separation of concerns, and testability;

Understanding of observability and monitoring in production systems.

We appreciate if you have those personal features:

Strong ownership of assigned initiatives;

Ability to work independently on both trivial and non-trivial tasks;

Effective cross-team coordination and collaboration;

Attention to clean, readable, and maintainable code. 

We are seeking those who align with our core values:

GROWE TOGETHER: Our team is our main asset. We work together and support each other to achieve our common goals;

DRIVE RESULT OVER PROCESS: We set ambitious, clear, measurable goals in line with our strategy and driving Growe to success;

BE READY FOR CHANGE: We see challenges as opportunities to grow and evolve. We adapt today to win tomorrow.

Growe welcomes those who are excited to:

Design, build, and maintain backend services using .NET (C#);

Develop and evolve microservices in a production environment;

Support existing functionality and ensure backward compatibility of releases;

Participate in task analysis, decomposition, and effort estimation;

Deliver completed tasks for testing and collaborate with QA during test phases;

Build integrations using asynchronous communication and event-driven patterns;

Work with AI integrations;

Identify performance bottlenecks and contribute to system design improvements;

Contribute to service observability (logs, metrics, traces, dashboards, monitoring);

Manage deployment configurations and manifests in Kubernetes environments;

Work in a GitOps setup and participate in deployment and operational ownership;

Collaborate with DevOps teams on infrastructure-related changes (including Terraform workflows);

Participate in on-call rotation and handle production incidents;

Identify technical debt and propose improvements;

Perform high-quality code reviews focusing on maintainability, performance, and consistency.

We need your professional experience:

5+ years of commercial backend development experience with C# / .NET, .NET Core / ASP.NET Core;

1+ year of experience with Java;

Solid understanding of microservices architecture and distributed systems;

Experience with asynchronous communication and event-driven architectures;

Experience with message brokers (Kafka or similar);

Strong experience with relational databases, especially PostgreSQL, including query optimization, indexing, performance tuning, and data modelling;

Experience writing Unit and Integration tests;

Good understanding of software design principles (SOLID, separation of concerns, testability);

Understanding of observability and monitoring in production systems;

Experience with AWS, Kubernetes, and Terraform will be a plus;

Experience with Prometheus, Loki, Tempo will be a plus;

Readiness to work with Java-based Kafka collectors/services containing business logic will be a strong plus;

Experience with AI integrations, LLM-based solutions, or GenAI-related tooling will be considered an important advantage.

We appreciate if you have those personal features:

Strive to learn new technologies/languages to solve non-standard challenges;

Good communication skills;

Multitasking, quick task execution;

Good team player;

Responsibility.

We are seeking those who align with our core values:

GROWE TOGETHER: Our team is our main asset. We work together and support each other to achieve our common goals;

DRIVE RESULT OVER PROCESS: We set ambitious, clear, measurable goals in line with our strategy and driving Growe to success;

BE READY FOR CHANGE: We see challenges as opportunities to grow and evolve. We adapt today to win tomorrow.
